-- ============================================================
-- SEED EXT 4: Módulo 24 — Discourse Markers (ex 154-220)
-- Novos tópicos: DMs em academic paragraph structure, DMs de
-- hedging e concession avançados, DMs entre parágrafos, DMs
-- em TOEFL essays (introduction, body, conclusion)
-- ============================================================
DO $$
DECLARE cid TEXT;
BEGIN
  SELECT id INTO cid FROM contents WHERE id = 'discourse-markers';
  IF cid IS NULL THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Módulo discourse-markers não encontrado'; END IF;

  INSERT INTO exercises (content_id, block_number, exercise_number, type, question, answer, options, explanation, difficulty) VALUES

  -- BLOCK 41: DMs de elaboração e exemplificação avançados
  (cid,41,154,'multiple_choice','Which discourse marker pair BEST introduces an example followed by a generalization?','"For instance... more broadly..." (specific → general)','["Furthermore... In addition...","For instance... more broadly...","However... Although...","Therefore... Thus..."]','"For instance" = example. "More broadly" = generalization back out.','medium'),
  (cid,41,155,'gap_fill','The policy has had mixed results. _____ specifically, emissions in the industrial sector _____ (fall), _____ agricultural emissions _____ (increase) significantly.','More / fell / while / increased',NULL,'"More specifically" for elaboration + "while" for contrast within the elaboration.','medium'),
  (cid,41,156,'gap_fill','Several mechanisms have been proposed. _____ illustration, one model _____ (suggest) that feedback loops _____ (amplify) initial disturbances; _____ words, small changes can have large systemic consequences.','By way of / suggests / amplify / in other',NULL,'"By way of illustration" + "in other words" for explanation.','hard'),
  (cid,41,157,'multiple_choice','Which marker introduces a SPECIFIC CASE that TYPIFIES a broader pattern?','Nowhere is this more evident than in the case of Singapore, where...','["On the contrary, Singapore shows...","Nowhere is this more evident than in the case of Singapore, where...","By contrast, Singapore demonstrates...","As a result, Singapore exemplifies..."]','"Nowhere is this more evident than in" = emphatic case marker that introduces a typical/extreme exemplar.','hard'),
  (cid,41,158,'gap_fill','Economic development _____ (not/always/accompany/passive) by improvements in human welfare. _____ case in point _____ the rapid industrialization of the Pearl River Delta, where GDP growth _____ (not/translate into) immediate improvements in living standards for all.','is not always accompanied / A / is / did not translate into',NULL,'"A case in point" = specific illustrating example.','hard'),

  -- BLOCK 42: DMs de contraste e concession avançados
  (cid,42,159,'gap_fill','The study reported strong positive results. _____ said, its methodology has _____ (subject/passive) to criticism.','That / been subjected',NULL,'"That said" = concessive DM that introduces a qualification of the preceding claim.','medium'),
  (cid,42,160,'gap_fill','The evidence in favor of the hypothesis is compelling. _____ _____, significant questions remain about its generalizability.','Even so',NULL,'"Even so" = concessive: accepts the preceding point but introduces a limitation.','easy'),
  (cid,42,161,'multiple_choice','Which concessive discourse marker is MOST FORMAL in academic writing?','Notwithstanding the evidence presented above, the authors'' conclusions warrant further scrutiny.','["But the evidence above, the authors'' conclusions need more scrutiny.","Notwithstanding the evidence presented above, the authors'' conclusions warrant further scrutiny.","Even though the evidence above, the authors'' conclusions need scrutiny.","Although, the evidence above, the authors'' conclusions warrant scrutiny."]','"Notwithstanding" = highly formal concessive preposition/discourse marker.','hard'),
  (cid,42,162,'gap_fill','The intervention _____ (produce) significant short-term results. _____ _____ apparent success, long-term data _____ (not yet/demonstrate/passive) sustained impact.','produced / Despite this / have not yet been demonstrated',NULL,'"Despite this apparent success" = concessive with demonstrative.','hard'),
  (cid,42,163,'gap_fill','Some scholars _____ (argue) that the welfare state is fiscally unsustainable. _____ _____, others _____ (contend) that investment in social protection _____ (actually/enhance) long-term productivity and reduce inequality.','argue / By contrast / contend / actually enhances',NULL,'"By contrast" = contrast DM between two opposing academic positions.','medium'),
  (cid,42,164,'multiple_choice','When is "admittedly" used as a discourse marker?','To concede a point before offering a counterargument.','["To add a further supporting point","To concede a point before offering a counterargument.","To introduce an example","To summarize a previous point"]','"Admittedly" = "I admit/concede that X is true, but..." = formal concessive.','medium'),

  -- BLOCK 43: DMs de consequência e resultado avançados
  (cid,43,165,'gap_fill','The population _____ (triple) in under two decades. _____ _____ result, infrastructure _____ (severely/strain/passive), and public services _____ (become) increasingly overwhelmed.','tripled / As a / was severely strained / became',NULL,'"As a result" = consequence DM for cause-effect chain.','easy'),
  (cid,43,166,'gap_fill','Carbon emissions _____ (continue) to rise. _____ _____ _____, the IPCC _____ (project) that warming will exceed 2°C by 2100.','continue / By extension / projects',NULL,'"By extension" = extrapolation DM (the implication follows logically from the fact).','hard'),
  (cid,43,167,'multiple_choice','Which consequence marker is MOST APPROPRIATE in a TOEFL academic essay?','Consequently, the implementation of stricter regulations appears warranted.','["So, stricter regulations seem to be a good idea.","As a result, we should make stricter regulations.","Consequently, the implementation of stricter regulations appears warranted.","That''s why stricter regulations are needed."]','"Consequently" = formal academic consequence DM.','easy'),
  (cid,43,168,'gap_fill','The devaluation _____ (increase) export competitiveness. _____ _____, import prices _____ (rise), _____ (erode) the real wages of workers dependent on imported goods.','increased / In turn / rose / eroding',NULL,'"In turn" = chain consequence DM. Participial "eroding" for result clause.','hard'),

  -- BLOCK 44: DMs de estrutura de parágrafo (topic/elaboration/conclusion)
  (cid,44,169,'gap_fill','This section examines the environmental consequences of rapid urbanization. _____ specific attention _____ (give/passive) to the effects on biodiversity, water quality, and urban heat islands.','Particular / is given',NULL,'Particular/special attention is given to = transition DM for focusing attention within a paragraph.','hard'),
  (cid,44,170,'gap_fill','_____ the foregoing analysis, it _____ (can/argue/passive) that the relationship between X and Y _____ (be) more complex than previously assumed.','In light of / can be argued / is',NULL,'"In light of the foregoing" = retrospective DM before a conclusion.','hard'),
  (cid,44,171,'multiple_choice','Which discourse marker BEST signals that the writer is about to QUALIFY A GENERAL STATEMENT?','While this characterization is broadly accurate, important exceptions exist.','["Furthermore, this characterization is broadly accurate.","While this characterization is broadly accurate, important exceptions exist.","As a result, this characterization is broadly accurate.","For example, this characterization is broadly accurate."]','"While" (at the start) = concessive qualification of a preceding or upcoming claim.','medium'),
  (cid,44,172,'gap_fill','The preceding paragraphs _____ (establish) that social capital and economic development _____ (relate). The _____ _____ _____ consider what policies _____ (most/effective/prove/passive) at building social capital.','have established / are related / following section will / have proved most effective',NULL,'Transition DM: "The following section will" = organizational announcement.','hard'),
  (cid,44,173,'multiple_choice','Which phrase best functions as a BETWEEN-PARAGRAPH TRANSITION?','The previous section established the theoretical framework; this section applies it to three case studies.','["In conclusion, this section applies the framework to three case studies.","The previous section established the theoretical framework; this section applies it to three case studies.","However, the framework can be applied to three case studies.","As a result, this section applies the framework to three case studies."]','Forward-backward link: "The previous section... this section..." = standard paragraph bridge.','medium'),

  -- BLOCK 45: TOEFL Reading
  (cid,45,174,'multiple_choice','[TOEFL Reading] "Despite significant advances in medical technology, life expectancy improvements have plateaued in several high-income countries." "Despite" introduces:','A concession acknowledging progress before pointing to a limitation.','["A result of the advances","A concession acknowledging progress before pointing to a limitation.","An example of life expectancy","A definition of medical technology"]','"Despite + NP" = concessive: acknowledges the advances but introduces the limitation.','easy'),
  (cid,45,175,'gap_fill','[TOEFL Reading] "The evidence broadly supports the proposed mechanism. _____, alternative explanations _____ (not/rule out/passive) on current data alone." Best DM and form?','Nevertheless / cannot be ruled out',NULL,'"Nevertheless" = strong concessive DM acknowledging what has been said but maintaining opposition.','medium'),
  (cid,45,176,'multiple_choice','[TOEFL Reading] "In short, the data suggests that X is causally linked to Y." "In short" signals:','A summary or restatement of the main point of the preceding analysis.','["A new example","A contrast","A summary or restatement of the main point of the preceding analysis.","A condition"]','"In short" / "In summary" = concluding/synthesizing DM.','easy'),
  (cid,45,177,'gap_fill','[TOEFL Reading] "The reforms were ambitious. _____ the same time, they faced fierce political resistance. _____ result, implementation _____ (proceed) far more slowly than originally anticipated." Best DMs?','At / As a / proceeded',NULL,'"At the same time" = simultaneous contrast. "As a result" = consequence.','medium'),

  -- BLOCK 46: TOEFL Speaking
  (cid,46,178,'production','[TOEFL Speaking — 45s] Summarize a reading on urban air quality and a lecture critiquing the reading''s solutions. Use discourse markers: however, while, that said, by contrast, consequently, in addition.','',NULL,'The reading argues that stricter vehicle emission standards represent the most effective policy tool for improving urban air quality, citing evidence from several European cities where post-regulation air quality improved significantly. The lecture, however, complicates this picture in several important ways. While vehicle emissions are certainly a significant contributor to urban pollution, the professor argues that industrial emissions and agricultural waste burning contribute comparably in many regions where the reading''s evidence does not apply. By contrast, in East Asian cities where residential heating and cooking fuel combustion are dominant pollution sources, vehicle standards would have relatively limited impact. That said, the lecture does not dismiss vehicle regulation entirely; it argues rather that comprehensive air quality policy requires a diagnostic approach that identifies the dominant local sources and targets them specifically, rather than applying a universal solution. Consequently, the reading''s policy recommendation appears too narrow.','hard'),
  (cid,46,179,'production','[TOEFL Speaking — 45s] Discuss whether technology improves or harms human connection. Use discourse markers for both sides: on the one hand/on the other hand, that said, nevertheless, by contrast.','',NULL,'The question of whether digital technology enhances or degrades human connection is genuinely complex, and the most accurate answer depends substantially on how connection is defined and measured. On the one hand, technology has undeniably extended the capacity of individuals to maintain contact across geographic distance, enabling relationships between family members, friends, and professional colleagues that geography would previously have made difficult or impossible. By contrast, critics argue that digital communication lacks the depth, trust, and sense of presence that characterizes meaningful in-person relationships, and that the quantity of digital contact has increased at the expense of the quality of face-to-face interaction. That said, the evidence on whether screen time actually reduces in-person social interaction is more mixed than popular discourse suggests: some studies find that heavy social media users also maintain more active offline social networks. Nevertheless, concerns about the attention economy''s design — which deliberately exploits psychological vulnerabilities to maximize engagement — represent a legitimate challenge to the claim that technology is neutral with respect to human connection.','hard'),

  -- BLOCK 47: TOEFL Writing
  (cid,47,180,'production','[TOEFL Writing — 150 words] Write an introduction for a TOEFL essay on "Are economic sanctions an effective foreign policy tool?" Use: discourse markers for framing, concession, and thesis statement.','',NULL,'Economic sanctions have become one of the most frequently deployed instruments of modern foreign policy, employed by major powers as an alternative to military intervention in attempts to change the behavior of states that violate international norms. At first glance, the case for sanctions appears straightforward: they inflict economic costs without the human costs of armed conflict and signal international disapproval without requiring the resource commitments of military engagement. Nevertheless, the historical record of sanctions effectiveness is considerably more mixed than their frequency of use might suggest, and scholars have identified numerous cases in which sanctions failed to produce the policy changes they targeted while inflicting disproportionate harm on civilian populations. This essay argues that while sanctions can play a legitimate role in foreign policy under specific conditions, they are most effective when precisely targeted, multilaterally coordinated, and accompanied by clear, achievable demands and credible diplomatic pathways to their removal.','hard'),
  (cid,47,181,'production','[TOEFL Writing — Error Correction] Fix discourse marker errors: "However, technology has many benefits. Also, however, there are risks. On the contrary to what critics say, most users benefit. Nevertheless the risks are real. Despite of the benefits, problems exist."','',NULL,'However x2 = do not repeat; use Furthermore/In addition for second point; Also, however = redundant (use one or the other); On the contrary → In contrast or Contrary to what critics say (''on the contrary'' is for contradicting, not comparing); Nevertheless the risks → Nevertheless, the risks (comma required after nevertheless); Despite of → Despite (despite + NP, no ''of''; ''in spite of'' does take ''of'').','hard'),

  -- BLOCK 48: Consolidação final
  (cid,48,182,'production','[TOEFL Writing — 200 words] Write a body paragraph on the role of education in reducing inequality. Use at least 8 different discourse markers appropriately.','',NULL,'At first glance, education appears to offer a straightforward mechanism for reducing economic inequality: by equipping individuals with productive skills, educational systems should, in principle, enable those born into disadvantaged circumstances to compete on more equal terms in the labor market. In practice, however, the relationship between educational expansion and inequality reduction has proven considerably more complex. On the one hand, educational attainment has risen across most income groups in the past century, and there is strong evidence that returns to education — measured in lifetime earnings — remain positive in most contexts. Nevertheless, despite this general trend, the distribution of educational quality remains deeply unequal within most societies: schools serving disadvantaged communities typically have fewer resources, less experienced teachers, and larger class sizes than those serving affluent areas. Consequently, expanding educational access without simultaneously addressing these quality disparities may actually reinforce inequality by widening the gap between the most and least advantaged. Furthermore, education alone cannot compensate for structural inequalities in wages, asset distribution, and access to professional networks that shape economic outcomes independently of educational credentials. In short, education is necessary but insufficient as a vehicle for achieving meaningful reductions in economic inequality.','hard'),
  (cid,48,183,'production','[TOEFL Speaking — 60s] Discuss the role of the arts in education. Use a wide range of discourse markers: purpose (in order to), concession (that said), addition (moreover), contrast (on the other hand), consequence (as a result), exemplification (for instance).','',NULL,'The question of how much space arts education should occupy in school curricula is frequently framed as a zero-sum competition with STEM subjects for limited instructional time and budget. In order to evaluate this framing, it is worth examining what arts education actually contributes to student development rather than assuming the answer in advance. Research suggests that sustained engagement with music, visual arts, drama, and dance develops capacities that transfer across domains: creative problem-solving, tolerance for ambiguity, capacity for self-expression, and the ability to interpret and communicate through non-verbal channels. For instance, studies of students enrolled in intensive music programs have found improved spatial reasoning and enhanced phonological awareness — capacities directly relevant to mathematics and literacy respectively. On the other hand, arts education does require resources, and in contexts where students are failing to achieve basic literacy and numeracy, it may be difficult to justify arts investment as a priority. That said, the evidence on arts integration — embedding arts-based learning within academic subjects rather than treating it as a separate domain — suggests that arts and academic learning need not compete. As a result, the question is less whether arts belong in schools and more how they are most effectively integrated with other learning goals. Moreover, the long-term returns — in terms of cultural vitality, civic engagement, and individual well-being — are real but difficult to quantify.','hard')

  ON CONFLICT (content_id, block_number, exercise_number) DO NOTHING;
END $$;
